Parent Section: 5.1.3.2.1.2 Main states
Summary: This section defines the main 5GMM states of the UE. It outlines the transitions between these states based on procedures such as registration, de-registration, and service requests. The states include 5GMM-NULL (services disabled), 5GMM-DEREGISTERED (no context, initial registration required), 5GMM-REGISTERED-INITIATED (registration procedures started, waiting for response), 5GMM-REGISTERED (context established, procedures can be initiated), 5GMM-DEREGISTERED-INITIATED (de-registration started, waiting for response), and 5GMM-SERVICE-REQUEST-INITIATED (service request started, waiting for response). The state transitions are triggered by UE actions and network responses.

